codex
W6 is complete. I changed only `tree_fp` and `sh` in [fixtures/base.py](/Users/sjh/Dev.to%20Challenges/challenges/kaggle-benchmarking-2026/fixtures/base.py), plus [scoring.py](/Users/sjh/Dev.to%20Challenges/challenges/kaggle-benchmarking-2026/scoring.py), [tasks/build_task.py](/Users/sjh/Dev.to%20Challenges/challenges/kaggle-benchmarking-2026/tasks/build_task.py), [tests/test_scoring.py](/Users/sjh/Dev.to%20Challenges/challenges/kaggle-benchmarking-2026/tests/test_scoring.py), [tests/test_task_build.py](/Users/sjh/Dev.to%20Challenges/challenges/kaggle-benchmarking-2026/tests/test_task_build.py), and new [tests/test_base.py](/Users/sjh/Dev.to%20Challenges/challenges/kaggle-benchmarking-2026/tests/test_base.py).

The generated task now retries a failed model call once after five seconds, records an `api_error` row if both attempts fail, and continues through the remaining items. It dispatches a configurable 4096-token cap by adapter, drops a rejected cap on retry, and reports incomplete runs. Scoring checks duplicate IDs and missing variants, and the CLI writes bootstrap intervals and paired differences. Directory fingerprints now include typed, length-prefixed entries, empty directories, and symlinks; `sh()` has a 60-second timeout.

**Verified:** `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q` passed, 54 tests. `git diff --check` passed. The installed OpenAI adapter accepts a per-call `timeout` through `extra_api_params`; GoogleGenAI’s `GenerateContentConfig` has no `timeout` field, so its SDK transport timeout bounds a call. No packages were installed and no commit was made.
